WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.170
A warm garden, far from home.

2
00:00:03.220 --> 00:00:05.040
One bright flower.

3
00:00:05.090 --> 00:00:08.650
A man sits beside it,
thinking of somewhere else.

4
00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:11.840
"Oh, to be in England", he sighs.

5
00:00:11.890 --> 00:00:16.820
And he pictures it: an orchard,
a hedge, a chaffinch on a bough.

6
00:00:16.870 --> 00:00:18.320
Leaves on the elm.

7
00:00:18.370 --> 00:00:20.770
A thrush singing each song twice.

8
00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:23.370
A pear-tree in blossom by the hedge.

9
00:00:23.420 --> 00:00:24.800
He isn't even there.

10
00:00:24.850 --> 00:00:27.980
So why does England sound like paradise?

11
00:00:28.030 --> 00:00:30.210
In this mission, you'll
meet Robert Browning,

12
00:00:30.260 --> 00:00:34.690
who published it in 1845,
after two visits to Italy.

13
00:00:34.740 --> 00:00:39.170
You'll hear how exclamations and dashes
make it sound like excited, unplanned

14
00:00:39.220 --> 00:00:40.120
speech.

15
00:00:40.170 --> 00:00:43.000
And you'll wait for the very last line.

16
00:00:43.050 --> 00:00:44.600
What does it change?

17
00:00:44.650 --> 00:00:48.560
Your mission: explain why
England sounds like paradise.
